---
import { DOCS, MIGRATION_PROMPT, SWITCH_STEPS, SWITCH_TOOLS, YOUTRACK_LINKS } from '@lib/compare/youtrack-alternative';
---

<section id="yt-switch" class="border-t border-line bg-app" aria-labelledby="yt-switch-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5 min-w-0">
      <h2 id="yt-switch-title" class="h2">
        Switching, with you reviewing every mapping.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        Both products speak MCP, so one agent can read your unresolved YouTrack work and recreate the supported parts
        here: projects, members, tags and issues. It is a guided move by prompt, not a one-click importer.
      </p>
      <ol class="steps-list mt-8 prose text-base">
        {SWITCH_STEPS.map(step => (
          <li>
            <strong>{step.title}.</strong> {step.body}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
      <div class="tabs">
        <div class="tabpanel-bar">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">A review-first migration prompt</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="yt-prompt">
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre
          id="yt-prompt"
          class="config yt-prompt"
          tabindex="0"
          aria-label="Migration prompt"
          set:text={MIGRATION_PROMPT}
        />
      </div>

      <h3 class="h3 mt-10">What the agent uses</h3>
      <p class="prose text-base mt-2">
        On this side, documented tools that act with your role and your token’s scopes. On the YouTrack side, its own
        MCP server with your permissions there.
      </p>
      <ul class="yt-tools mt-4" aria-label="Nothing Left tools">
        {SWITCH_TOOLS.map(tool => (
          <li>
            <code>{tool}</code>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h3 class="h3 mt-10">What to expect</h3>
      <ul class="rule-list mt-3">
        <li class="py-4 prose text-base">
          Issues are created by you, now. Their full history, original timestamps and workflow state stay in YouTrack.
        </li>
        <li class="py-4 prose text-base">
          Attachments, time records and articles are not part of the prompt above; move them only once the issues are
          right.
        </li>
        <li class="py-4 prose text-base">
          For a bulk move, use the generic CSV import. A native YouTrack importer is not built.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href={DOCS.mcp}>
          Connecting an AI agent
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="link" href={YOUTRACK_LINKS.mcp} rel="noopener">
          YouTrack’s MCP server
          <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
            ↗
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .yt-prompt {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .yt-tools {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .yt-tools code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
  }
</style>
